# Build and tooling

## Toolchain status

- Swift via **Command Line Tools only** (`/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools`). There is no Xcode, so no `xcodebuild`, no
  `-create-xcframework`, and no `.xcodeproj`/asset catalogs/`.xcstrings`. Everything builds with `swift build` and shell scripts.
- **No Rust / Cargo / UniFFI.** The core is pure Swift (+ thin C IOKit bridge). Do not add a Rust toolchain dependency.
- Homebrew is available, but builds must not depend on brew libraries.
- XCTest is unavailable without Xcode — use `naga-core-smoke` for golden checks.

## Pipeline

1. `cd app && swift build` — builds `NagaUSB`, `NagaCore`, `NagaCLI`, `NagaTrinityControl`.
2. `swift run` / `swift run naga-cli …` for quick iteration.
3. `scripts/bundle-app.sh`: `swift build -c release --arch arm64` → assemble `build/Naga Trinity Control.app`
   (`Contents/MacOS`, `Contents/Resources` with the SwiftPM resource bundle, `Info.plist` with `CFBundleIdentifier=local.naga-trinity-control`,
   `LSMinimumSystemVersion=13.0`, `NSHumanReadableCopyright`, LaunchAgent plist in `Contents/Library/LaunchAgents/`)
   → `codesign --force --deep -s - "<app>"`.

The app must run from the `.app` bundle (TCC, login items and `Bundle.main` resources depend on it). `swift run` is only for
quick UI iteration without hotkeys or a login item.

## Verification checklist (no automated hardware CI)

- `./scripts/test-core.sh` (golden bytes + migration + apply settle).
- `swift build` with zero errors.
- With the mouse plugged in: `naga-cli info` → `naga-cli rgb static #ff0000` → `naga-cli apply` → app "Send to mouse",
  lock/unlock, sleep/wake, macro on side button 1. Report the results to the user; never claim hardware behavior you didn't observe.

## Repo hygiene

Gitignore `app/.build/`, `build/`, `.upstream/`, `*.xcuserstate`, `.DS_Store`.
